title: Judiciary Reform
new-page: true
is-card: true
view-if: psoe_in_government = 1 and justice_minister_party = "PSOE" and judiciary_timer = 0
on-arrival: month_actions += 1; judiciary_timer += 6
card-image: img/portraits/delosrios.jpg
tags: govt_affairs, cabinet

= Judiciary Reform

The Judiciary is one of the most reactionary and traditionalist pillars of the state, closely tied to the monarchist establishment and the latifundistas. Many magistrates and judges have held office since the days of Alfonso XIII. While they often show extreme leniency toward right-wing conspirators and reactionary plotters, they ruthlessly persecute labor unionists, anarchists and leftist agitators.

[? if judicial_reform <= 0 : There is a growing demand within our allies and our own party for a 'republicanization' of the justice system, though attempting this will face a fierce resistance from the judiciary and right-wing republicans. ?]
[? if judicial_reform == 1 : We have initiated reforms to clean up the courts, but many entrenched reactionary magistrates still remain in key positions. More work is urgently needed before conservative forces take power and roll them back. ?]
[? if judicial_reform >= 2 : We have successfully carried out significant judicial reforms. At the very least, the courts are no longer actively sabotaging the democratic regime or shielding the enemies of the Republic. ?]

- @reform: Carry out substantial judicial reforms.
- @minor_reforms: Carry out minor judicial reforms.
- @as_is: Leave the judiciary as it is.
- @cancel_advisor_action

@reform
subtitle: -1 budget
unavailable-subtitle: Not enough budget.
choose-if: budget >= 1
on-arrival: budget -= 1; democratization += 2; coalition_dissent += 1 if in_republican_socialist_conjunction == 1; workers_psoe += 5*(1-dissent) if democratization >= 3; middle_psoe += 5*(1-dissent) if democratization >= 3; rural_psoe += 5*(1-dissent) if democratization >= 3; judicial_reform += 2; pro_republic += 5*(1-dissent); coup_progress += 1

We push for the replacement of biased, anti-republican magistrates with progressive, democratic jurists, and modernize the legal codes. This bold attempt to democratize the courts sparks furious backlash from conservative circles [? if in_republican_socialist_conjunction = 1: and the PRR ?].

@minor_reforms
on-arrival: democratization += 1; middle_psoe += 2*(1-dissent) if democratization >= 3; judicial_reform += 1; pro_republic += 3*(1-dissent); judiciary_timer += 6

We target only the most flagrantly corrupt or openly anti-republican judges, leaving the core judicial structure intact. Reforming the system this way is painfully slow, but it avoids an immediate institutional crisis.

@as_is
go-to: root
